& [Fold1Identity] distinguishes semantic and contract identity
  + one type identity may have input, output, or both direction-qualified definition identities

& [Fold2Boundary] isolates accepted from emitted shape
  + Deserialize universe and Serialize universe are separate closed local-reference graphs
  + no reference or cache reuse crosses the boundary

& [Fold3Data] makes direction inspectable
  + direction enum, two definition maps, contract accounts, raw digests, contract fingerprints, residuals, and compatibility classifications

& [Fold4Behavior] is direction-first generation
  + select direction, select contract, derive closure, normalize, account, domain-separate, fingerprint, bundle, and report

& [Fold5Failure] attacks conflation
  + missing direction, wrong cache, cross-universe reference, crossing type with one identity, ambiguous preimage, and unclassified golden drift

& [Fold6Proof] exercises both sides
  + exact assignments, isolated closure, PreparedRunRequest dual fixtures, raw-equality reporting, fingerprint inequality, serde agreement, and same-direction compatibility

& [Fold7Growth] adds no runtime authority
  + profile may unlock a separately signed CPMS-I02 capability slice
  + it does not unlock validator, provider projection, model execution, service, effect, or hardware

